# A name is read off a constructor function and called. Nobody has laid `call` on Base, on Animal or on Dog, so the lookup ends at Function.prototype. `of` and `init` lie on the function itself, `create` on the function above Dog.
# Nothing of that is proven. The record of the class expects it, and the guard of the name on the side of the function object answers for it from the first look until somebody changes what a lookup finds.
